<code>assert this.isEmpty() || (this.peek() == null && this.getFirst() == null) || this.peek().equals(this.getFirst());</code>

However, given the nature of the `peek` method and the fact that it returns `null` if the list is empty, we can simplify the assertion to:

<code>assert this.peek() == null || this.peek().equals(this.getFirst());</code>

This captures the essence of the comment: if the list is not empty, the result of `peek()` should be equal to the first element of the list. If the list is empty, `peek()` will return `null`.
